LC 14 — Longest Common Prefix
Pattern:String Traversal

Logic:
Take the first string as prefix.
Compare it with every other string.
Keep reducing prefix until it matches.

Algorithm:
prefix = first string

For every other string:
    while string doesn't start with prefix:
        remove last character from prefix

return prefix

CODE:
class Solution {
public:
    string longestCommonPrefix(vector<string>& strs) {
        string prefix = strs[0];

        for (int i = 1; i < strs.size(); i++) {
            while (strs[i].find(prefix) != 0)
                prefix.pop_back();

            if (prefix.empty())
                return "";
        }

        return prefix;
    }
};

EX:
s = ["flower","flow","flight"]

prefix = "flower"

Compare with "flow"
→ reduce → "flow"

Compare with "flight"
→ reduce → "fl"

Answer = "fl" ✅
